# Nathan AI 🚀 — AI Texting & Work Vault (additive prototype)
This module expands the existing Assistant, Research Workspace and Deep Archive rather than replacing them. Launch [index.html](./index.html) from the Nathan AI Main Hub.

## Implemented
- Manually capture AI texting, prompts, responses, code, research and creative work with a title, type and source label.
- Explicitly import owner-selected files of arbitrary MIME type up to 20 MB each. Store original File/Blob in local IndexedDB, retaining binary bytes.
- Search locally by title, source, type and a capped textual preview; inspect a short excerpt and download original content.
- Export a metadata-only JSON manifest; delete selected local entries with confirmation.

## Honest boundaries
- No automatic access to ChatGPT/Codex/Sider/other providers, history synchronization, autonomous file capture or external filesystem scanning.
- Local IndexedDB storage is **not encrypted**, authenticated or guaranteed persistent. Private data should be backed up securely and should not be committed to this **public** repo.
- Exported manifest **does not** back up file bytes. Download originals individually; full vault backup/import and encrypted/synced storage require a separate version.
- No LLM is invoked. Existing optional model adapter remains the Assistant's separate opt-in facility.
- Additional future work: project folders, tagging, provenance graph, opt-in provider connector permissions, full binary backup/restore, encryption and quotas, deduplication, conflict resolution and audited cross-device sync.

## Source policy
Keep creator-authored words verbatim in original records. Analyses, verified statements and derived interpretations remain separate. Preserve the root Codex 141-byte declaration, all prior app components, and 0/1 whole-state conventions.
